    "html": "<section><div class=\"ip-inner\"><ol class=\"ip-steps\"><li><h3>Read the record</h3><p>See how your members voted on every roll call, each linked to its official source.</p><div class=\"ip-links\"><a class=\"btn-text\" href=\"/my-representative\">Find my reps</a></div></li><li><h3>Write to your rep</h3><p>Start from the facts of a vote, add your own words, and send it yourself.</p><div class=\"ip-links\"><a class=\"btn-text\" href=\"/this-week\">Pick a vote</a></div></li><li><h3>See how they vote next</h3><p>Check This week to see what reaches the floor next and how each member voted.</p><div class=\"ip-links\"><a class=\"btn-text\" href=\"/this-week\">This week</a></div></li></ol><p class=\"ip-loop\">Then the next vote, and the loop starts again.</p></div></section><section><div class=\"ip-inner\"><h2>What’s Live Today</h2><ul class=\"ip-checks\"><li><a href=\"/my-representative\">Your representatives</a></li><li><a href=\"/this-week\">Every House and Senate roll call</a></li><li><a href=\"/bills\">Bills in plain English</a></li><li><a href=\"/this-week\">This week on the floor</a></li><li><a href=\"/my-representative\">A record in 60 seconds</a></li><li><a href=\"/this-week\">Tell your rep</a></li><li><a href=\"/developers\">Free API and MCP server</a></li></ul></div></section><section><div class=\"ip-inner\"><h2>AI Explains. It Never Speaks For Anyone.</h2><div class=\"ip-pair\"><div class=\"ip-pair-info\"><h3>We use AI to</h3><ul><li>Explain bills from their official text, with the source beside it</li><li>Narrate a member’s voting patterns from numbers we computed first</li><li>Answer your AI assistant with cited records through our MCP server</li></ul></div><div><h3>We never use AI to</h3><ul><li>Write in your representative’s voice or guess their positions</li><li>Send anything you haven’t read and approved</li><li>Choose a side for you, or rank and score constituents</li></ul></div></div></div></section><section><div class=\"ip-inner\"><h2>Go Deeper</h2><ul class=\"ip-index\"><li><a href=\"/data-sources\"><span class=\"ip-index-title\">How we get our data</span><span class=\"ip-index-dek\">Every source, what we take from it, and how often.</span></a></li><li><a href=\"/methodology\"><span class=\"ip-index-title\">Methodology</span><span class=\"ip-index-dek\">How each number and explanation is made.</span></a></li><li><a href=\"/about\"><span class=\"ip-index-title\">About BallotWatch</span><span class=\"ip-index-dek\">Independent, nonpartisan, and open source.</span></a></li></ul></div></section>",
    "markdown": "### Read the record\n\nSee how your members voted on every roll call, each linked to its official source.\n\n### Write to your rep\n\nStart from the facts of a vote, add your own words, and send it yourself.\n\n### See how they vote next\n\nCheck This week to see what reaches the floor next and how each member voted.\n\nThen the next vote, and the loop starts again.\n\n## What’s Live Today\n\n- [Your representatives](https://www.ballotwatch.io/my-representative)\n- [Every House and Senate roll call](https://www.ballotwatch.io/this-week)\n- [Bills in plain English](https://www.ballotwatch.io/bills)\n- [This week on the floor](https://www.ballotwatch.io/this-week)\n- [A record in 60 seconds](https://www.ballotwatch.io/my-representative)\n- [Tell your rep](https://www.ballotwatch.io/this-week)\n- [Free API and MCP server](https://www.ballotwatch.io/developers)\n\n## AI Explains. It Never Speaks For Anyone.\n\n### We use AI to\n\n- Explain bills from their official text, with the source beside it\n- Narrate a member’s voting patterns from numbers we computed first\n- Answer your AI assistant with cited records through our MCP server\n\n### We never use AI to\n\n- Write in your representative’s voice or guess their positions\n- Send anything you haven’t read and approved\n- Choose a side for you, or rank and score constituents\n\n## Go Deeper\n\n- [How we get our dataEvery source, what we take from it, and how often.](https://www.ballotwatch.io/data-sources)\n- [MethodologyHow each number and explanation is made.](https://www.ballotwatch.io/methodology)\n- [About BallotWatchIndependent, nonpartisan, and open source.](https://www.ballotwatch.io/about)"
